es for employees; 2) peocedures for supporting inclusive services to children with special care needs. The policy must address the requirements outlined in 746.2202.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026288346","violation_type_title":"Written Operational Policies - Support inclusive services (26 TAC §746.501(a)(30))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1090026-i20240702-v4","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-3407","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1090026-i20240702","date":"2024-07-02","original_code":"746.3407","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-07-08","finding":"Maintenance of Building, Grounds and Equipment: The top portion of the Dutch door on the front of the large playhouse has broken. There is a small wasp nest inside the playhouse.","topic":"facilities","source_record_id":"1026369141","violation_type_title":"Maintenance of Building, Grounds and Equipment (26 TAC §746.3407)","topic_label":"Facilities & equipment"}]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1090026-i20230815","date":"2023-08-15","inspection_type":"Inspection","result":"No deficiencies cited","passed":true,"violation_count":0,"open_count":0,"evidence_class":"VERIFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_record_id":"905797032","url":"https://data.texas.gov/resource/m5q4-3y3d.json?activity_id=905797032","retrieved_at":"2026-11-05T21:27:29.718Z","effective_date":"2023-08-15","evidence_class":"VERIFIED"},"occurrences":[]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1090026-i20220831","date":"2022-08-31","inspection_type":"Inspection","result":"Deficiencies cited","passed":false,"violation_count":5,"open_count":0,"evidence_class":"VERIFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_record_id":"905797031","url":"https://data.texas.gov/resource/m5q4-3y3d.json?activity_id=905797031","retrieved_at":"2026-11-05T21:27:29.718Z","effective_date":"2022-08-31","evidence_class":"VERIFIED"},"occurrences":[{"id":"tx-hhsc-1090026-i20220831-v1","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-4135-b","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1090026-i20220831","date":"2022-08-31","original_code":"746.4135(b)","severity":"medium","severity_label":"Medium risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2022-09-13","finding":"Children's Products- Annual Certification: The last documented review of the CPSC website to review the recall list to ensure no recalled items are in the center was observed 1/2021.  You must certify annually in writing using a form provided by DFPS that you have reviewed each of the recall notices issued by the CPSC and that there are no unsafe products in the center.","topic":"staffing","source_record_id":"1026535325","violation_type_title":"Children's Products- Annual Certification (26 TAC §746.4135(b))","topic_label":"Staff qualifications & clearances"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1090026-i20220831-v2","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-5202-2","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1090026-i20220831","date":"2022-08-31","original_code":"746.5202(2)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2022-09-06","finding":"Emergency Preparedness Plan - Communication Procedures: The Emergency Preparedness Plan was evaluated and lacked the following written procedures: 1) The emergency telephone number that is on file with Child Care Regulation; and 2) How you will communicate with local authorities, parents, and Child Care Regulation.","topic":"fire","source_record_id":"1026375178","violation_type_title":"Emergency Preparedness Plan - Communication Procedures (26 TAC §746.5202(2))","topic_label":"Fire safety & emergency drills"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1090026-i20220831-v3","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-603-a-4","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1090026-i20220831","date":"2022-08-31","original_code":"746.603(a)(4)","severity":"medium","severity_label":"Medium risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2022-09-19","finding":"Children's Records - Immunizations: A sampling of children records were evaluated. One child's immunization record was observed incomplete. One child's notarized Exemption from Immunizations for Reasons of Conscience form has expired. Each individual vaccine exemption affidavit is good for two years from the date notarized.","topic":"staffing","source_record_id":"1026334941","violation_type_title":"Children's Records - Immunizations (26 TAC §746.603(a)(4))","topic_label":"Staff qualifications & clearances"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1090026-i20220831-v4","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-901-4","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1090026-i20220831","date":"2022-08-31","original_code":"746.901(4)","severity":"medium_low","severity_label":"Medium-low risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2022-09-11","finding":"Required Personnel Records - Required Affidavit: One caregiver's record lacked a notarized affidavit.","topic":"staffing","source_record_id":"1026455120","violation_type_title":"Required Personnel Records - Required Affidavit (Form 2985) (26 TAC §746.901(4))","topic_label":"Staff qualifications & clearances"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1090026-i20220831-v5","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-501-a-18-f","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1090026-i20220831","date":"2022-08-31","original_code":"746.501(a)(18)(F)","severity":"medium","severity_label":"Medium risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2022-09-06","finding":"Written Operational Policies - Plan for Extreme Weather: The operational policies were evaluated and lacked the following written procedures: Promotion of indoor and outdoor physical activity that is consistent with Subchapter F of this chapter (relating to Developmental Activities and Activity Plan); your policies must include: (A) The benefits of physical activity and outdoor play; (B)  The type of physical activity (structured and unstructured) that children may engage in at your operation; (C) Each setting in which your physical activity program will take place; (D) The rec